{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Built-in-backends"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This backend supports Linux, macOS and Windows (maybe?), but its support for non-Linux platforms is significantly worse than ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s (due to underlying Gtk 3 issues). Even on Linux, it’s recommended to use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend"},{"type":"text","text":" over Gtk3Backend where possible."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-Linux Gtk3Backend support is not a priority of this backend, and should only be used during development (e.g. to test your Linux UI natively on a Mac). There are multiple better choices of backend available on each non-Linux platform.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Warning","style":"warning"},{"type":"heading","text":"System dependencies","level":2,"anchor":"System-dependencies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you can use Gtk3Backend you must install the required system dependencies for your platform.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Linux","level":3,"anchor":"Linux"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["sudo apt install libgtk-3-dev"],"syntax":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 1: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"installing Gtk 3 dev on an apt-based Linux distro","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you are on a non-apt distro and the Gtk3Backend requirements end up differing significantly from the requirements stated above, please open a GitHub issue or PR so that we can improve the documentation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"macOS","level":3,"anchor":"macOS"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["brew install pkg-config gtk+3"],"syntax":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Figure 2: ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"installing Gtk 3 using Homebrew","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t have Homebrew, installation instructions can be found at ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/brew.sh"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It should also be possible to use "},{"code":"gtk3","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" installed via MacPorts, but I have not tested that."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Windows","level":3,"anchor":"Windows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk3"},{"type":"text","text":" installation has not been tested on Windows, and neither has Gtk3Backend, although there shouldn’t be anything to stop it from working (🤞). Follow the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk4"},{"type":"text","text":" installation instructions from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and replace "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk3"},{"type":"text","text":" in any vcpkg commands or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vcpkg.json"},{"type":"text","text":" manifest files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you try this on Windows open a GitHub issue (even if it works without changes) so that we can fix any issues you faced and update this documentation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Usage","level":2,"anchor":"Usage"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["...","","let package = Package(","  ...","  targets: [","    ...","    .executableTarget(","      name: \"YourApp\",","      dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"SwiftCrossUI\", package: \"swift-cross-ui\"),","        .product(name: \"GtkBackend\", package: \"swift-cross-ui\"),","      ]","    )","    ...","  ]","  ...",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 3: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"adding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk3Backend"},{"type":"text","text":" to an executable target"}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftCrossUI","import Gtk3Backend","","@main","struct YourApp: App {","  \/\/ You can explicitly initialize your app's chosen backend if you desire.","  \/\/ This happens automatically when you import any of the built-in backends.","  \/\/","  \/\/ var backend = Gtk3Backend()","  \/\/","  \/\/ If you aren't using Swift Bundler, you may have to explicitly provide","  \/\/ your app's identifier for some Gtk3Backend features to work correctly","  \/\/ (such as handling custom URL schemes).","  \/\/","  \/\/ var backend = Gtk3Backend(appIdentifier: \"com.example.YourApp\")","","  var body: some Scene {","    WindowGroup {","      Text(\"Hello, World!\")","        .padding()","    }","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 4: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk3Backend"}]}]}]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Gtk3Backend","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/DefaultBackend","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/WinUIBackend","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/Swif